      "writtenOn": "2024-09-21T09:28:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The alternative would be safe:\n\n1. pull the IP header.\n2. depending on iph-\u003eprotocol, pull the UDP or TCP header.\n\nOr slight optimization if expecting lots of UDP traffic (unlikely)\n\n1. pull the IP+UDP header.\n2. if iph-\u003eprotocol says IPPROTO_TCP, pull the remaining TCP header.\n\nBut I understand that you want to optimize for the TCP fast path and only pull once for TCP. Unfortunately I see no way that that is ever safe for UDP traffic.",
